<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H12526</pnldref><english><title>Possess a psychoactive substance in a custodial institution</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>Drugs</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>misuse</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>drug</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>controlled</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>substance</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>high</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>legal high</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>legal highs</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>stimulate</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>stimulating</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>depress</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>depressing</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>mental</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>function</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>functioning</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>emotional</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>state</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>prison</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..) were in possession of a psychoactive substance, namely **(..IDENTIFY SUBSTANCE..), which you knew or suspected to be a psychoactive substance, in a custodial institution, namely **(..SPECIFY CUSTODIAL INSTITUTION..), with the intention of consuming it for its psychoactive effects</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to sections 9 and 10(2) of the Psychoactive Substances Act 2016.</legislation><pointstoprove>Date and Location&lt;br /&gt;possess psychoactive substance in custodial institution&lt;br /&gt;knows / suspects it is psychoactive substance&lt;br /&gt;intends to consume it for psychoactive effects</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA8</code><description>Consider PNC warning - 'Drugs'</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>(i) A custodial institution means any of the following -&lt;br /&gt;(a) a prison;&lt;br /&gt;(b) a young offender institution, secure training centre, secure college, young offenders institution, young offenders centre, juvenile justice centre or remand centre;&lt;br /&gt;(c) a removal centre, a short-term holding facility or pre-departure accommodation;&lt;br /&gt;(d) service custody premises</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofar